## Pull Request Workflow

### PR Creation Triggers
Open a PR when:
1. Workstream slice is complete (all acceptance criteria met)
2. All tests pass locally
3. Code is ready for review
4. You want feedback mid-slice (mark as "Draft")

### PR Creation Process

```bash
# 1. Ensure branch is pushed
git push origin wsX/<slice-name>

# 2. Open PR via GitHub CLI (recommended)
gh pr create --title "wsX: <Slice Description>" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Intent
<What this PR does and why>

## Workstream
<WS number and name from master plan>

## Owned Paths
<Files/directories this PR touches>

## Flags
<Feature flags used, defaults>

## Dependencies
<Any dependencies on other PRs/workstreams>

## Verification Steps
- [ ] Backend tests pass
- [ ] Frontend tests pass (if applicable)
- [ ] Staging smoke test: <specific test>

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] <Criterion 1 from master plan>
- [ ] <Criterion 2 from master plan>
- [ ] <Criterion 3 from master plan>

## Rollback Plan
<How to rollback if issues found>
EOF
)"

# 3. Or open via GitHub web UI
# Navigate to: https://github.com/hellogreencow/WatchfulEye-V2/compare/master...<branch-name>
```

### PR Template (Use `.github/pull_request_template.md`)

```markdown
## Intent
<!-- What this PR does and why (2-3 sentences) -->

## Workstream
<!-- e.g., WS4.1 — Enhance Examine Runner -->

## Owned Paths
<!-- Files/directories this PR modifies -->
- `watchfuleye/v3/investigations/`
- `tests/test_v3_examine_api.py`

## Explicitly NOT Touched
<!-- Hot files avoided -->
- `web_app.py` ✅ (not modified)
- `frontend/src/Dashboard.tsx` ✅ (not modified)

## Flags
<!-- Feature flags used and defaults -->
- `V3_EXAMINE_MVP` — default OFF

## Dependencies
<!-- Any dependencies on other PRs/workstreams -->
- Depends on: WS0 entity resolution (merged in PR #15)

## Verification Steps
- [ ] Backend: `ruff check && mypy watchfuleye && pytest`
- [ ] Frontend: `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm test`
- [ ] Staging: Deploy to `/opt/watchfuleye2-staging` and test `POST /api/v3/examine`

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Examine endpoint returns confidence intervals (0.0-1.0)
- [ ] Evidence ranked by trust score * recency
- [ ] Dissent section includes counter-evidence
- [ ] Tests verify all new behavior

## Rollback Plan
<!-- How to rollback if issues found -->
- Set `V3_EXAMINE_MVP=false` in staging env
- Or revert this PR's commits from master

## CodeRabbit Notes
<!-- Address CodeRabbit comments here or note "N/A" -->
```

