## Staging Deployment (After Merge)

### Deploy to Server Staging

```bash
# SSH to server
ssh <user>@<server>

# Navigate to staging worktree
cd /opt/watchfuleye2-staging

# Pull latest master (fast-forward only)
git pull --ff-only origin master

# Restart services
sudo systemctl restart watchfuleye-backend-staging
sudo systemctl restart watchfuleye-frontend-staging

# Verify
curl http://localhost:5004/api/health
curl http://localhost:3001/
```

### Staging Validation Checklist
- [ ] Backend health check passes
- [ ] Frontend serves correctly
- [ ] Feature flag can be toggled
- [ ] Feature works as expected (when flag ON)
- [ ] No regressions (when flag OFF)
- [ ] Logs show no errors

---

## Conflict Resolution

### If Merge Conflicts Occur:

```bash
# 1. Fetch latest master
git fetch origin master

# 2. Rebase onto master
git rebase origin/master

# 3. Resolve conflicts
# Edit conflicting files, remove conflict markers

# 4. Stage resolved files
git add <resolved-files>

# 5. Continue rebase
git rebase --continue

# 6. Force push (rebase rewrites history)
git push --force-with-lease origin wsX/<slice-name>
```

**Abort rebase if needed:**
```bash
git rebase --abort
```

---

## Emergency Rollback

### If Production Breaks After Merge:

**Option 1: Revert the Merge Commit**
```bash
# Find merge commit SHA
git log --oneline -10

# Revert it
git revert -m 1 <merge-commit-sha>

# Push
git push origin master
```

**Option 2: Flip Feature Flag OFF**
```bash
# SSH to server
ssh <user>@<server>

# Edit staging/prod env
# Set V3_<FEATURE>=false

# Restart services
sudo systemctl restart watchfuleye-backend
```

**Option 3: Emergency Hotfix PR**
- Create branch from master
- Fix issue
- Fast-track PR review
- Merge and deploy

